<p class="kicker">Scrapbook</p>

# Scrapbook

<p class="lead">Proposals, prototypes and variations, rendered before anything is decided. A design is worked out here, side by side, then built where it belongs.</p>

## What goes here

- **UI:** a new screen, a component, an interaction or a flow, in a few versions.
- **Communications:** a post, a key visual or a layout, in a few directions.
- **Brand:** a mark, a lockup, a colour or a type detail, when the brand itself is in question.

## How to file one

- Title it `Scrapbook/UI/<topic>`, `Scrapbook/Communications/<topic>` or `Scrapbook/Brand/<topic>`.
- Make one story per variation, named so they compare: `A · Compact`, `B · Spacious`.
- Build each from the real components, tokens, fonts and files, so what you compare is what would ship.
- Show both themes, and a phone width where it matters.

## When one is chosen

The chosen version is built in its own section, under **UI**, **Communications** or **Brand**. The others stay in the Scrapbook as a record until they're no longer useful.
